		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Co-ops or contractors for 3D physics simulation at AMD]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=33550#p33550"><![CDATA[
I am looking for co-ops or contractors for 3D physics simulation engineering at AMD. <br><br>Fluid simulation<br>1. Must have a solid background on Eulerian and Lagrangian approaches<br>2. Good understanding on two way interaction between fluid and rigid bodies <br>3. Surface reconstruction from particles such as anisotrophic approach<br>4. Should be able to implement latest fluid simulation based on published papers<br>5. GPGPU (OpenCL or CUDA) experience is highly desirable<br>6. C++ and object oriented programming<br>7. Cross platform development, CMake, build server, Maya plugin and python are good<br>7. UI/framework experience such as Qt or Image Engine's Gaffer is a good bonus<br><br>Rigidbody simulation<br>1. Will be working on Bullet so should be familiar with it<br>2. Expected to have an expertise in at least one of these areas: accurate collision detection or constraint solver<br>3. SSE/AVX or parallel process (CPU/GPU)<br><br>The office is located in Sunnyvale California USA and working onsite is preferable. Remote working will be considered based on the level of experience. <br><br>If you are interested, please send the email to dongsoo.han at amd dot com<br><br>Dongsoo Han<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8069">saggita</a> — Tue Jun 10, 2014 9:01 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
